    "descriptionEn": "> **Key takeaways**\n> - **Skate stoppers** are physical hardware fasteners that prevent skateboard, BMX, and inline-skate grinds on commercial and municipal property. The Canadian search term **'skate stoppers' (90/mo, LOW competition)** resolves to a procurement officer or property manager looking to retrofit ledges, planters, walls, and bench backs after vandalism damage. This is the most-specified line in the category — surface-mount, 316L marine-grade stainless, and engineered for the freeze-thaw cycle.\n> - Engineered for the Canadian climate (freeze-thaw, salt-air corrosion, frost-line anchoring) and supplied with stamped engineering for every climate zone.\n> - Standard procurement under $50K direct purchase, public RFP/DDP above $50K via MERX, BC Bid, or municipal portals.\n\n## What skate stoppers actually do\n\n**Skate stoppers** are physical hardware fasteners that prevent skateboard, BMX, and inline-skate grinds on commercial and municipal property. The Canadian search term **'skate stoppers' (90/mo, LOW competition)** resolves to a procurement officer or property manager looking to retrofit ledges, planters, walls, and bench backs after vandalism damage. This is the most-specified line in the category — surface-mount, 316L marine-grade stainless, and engineered for the freeze-thaw cycle. \n\n## Materials and finishes for Canadian climate\n\nCoastal cities like **Vancouver, Halifax, and Victoria** require **316 marine-grade stainless** because chloride salt-air pitting destroys 304 stainless within 5-7 years. Inland deployments in **Toronto, Calgary, Winnipeg, and Edmonton** use **304 stainless** with a brushed finish that hides scuff marks. For heritage-designated sites — **Vieux-Montréal, Parliament Hill, Citadel Halifax, Inner Harbour Victoria** — we offer a **bronze patina finish** approved by Heritage Conservation officers in those jurisdictions.\n\n## Install patterns by surface type\n\nFor **concrete planter walls and retaining walls**, we anchor with **3/8\\\" × 3-inch stainless wedge anchors** drilled to **75 mm** depth. **Granite and limestone ledges** use **stainless threaded inserts** in 12 mm cores — no surface staining. **Wood-capped masonry seating** receives **#14 × 65 mm stainless lag screws** through pre-drilled pilots. Every install includes a **post-install caulk seal** rated for Canadian freeze-thaw cycles down to **-40°C**.\n\n## Procurement and warranty\n\nWe respond to public RFP and DDP requests within 5 business days with stamped engineering, AODA / OBC code-conformance letters, climate-zone heatmaps for the destination city, and bonded-contractor accreditation for prevailing-wage municipal work. Install crews carry $5M general liability and are insured to work on TTC, STM, GO Transit, Metrolinx, and BC Transit properties. Warranty is 10 years on coatings and lifetime on 316L marine-grade structural elements. Volume pricing applies on orders of 20+ studs; bulk municipal orders typically land in the $24-32 per-stud installed range with quantity discounts. Most quotes return within 24 hours of address submission.\n\n## What this product is NOT for\n\nThese stoppers are **not** suitable for round handrails (use our **handrail clamps** instead) or for surfaces narrower than **80 mm** (use **edge strips**). For very long architectural ledges — say **over 6 metres continuous** — the edge strip is a more cost-effective install.",
    "descriptionFr": "> **Key takeaways**\n> - Les **bloque-skate** sont des fixations matérielles qui empêchent les glisses de skateboard, BMX et patins en ligne sur les propriétés commerciales et municipales canadiennes. Notre variante à plots est la gamme la plus spécifiée — fixation de surface, inox 316L grade marin, conçu pour les cycles gel-dégel.\n> - Engineered for the Canadian climate (freeze-thaw, salt-air corrosion, frost-line anchoring) and supplied with stamped engineering for every climate zone.\n> - Standard procurement under $50K direct purchase, public RFP/DDP above $50K via MERX, BC Bid, or municipal portals.\n\n## Ce que font les bloque-skate\n\nLes **bloque-skate** sont des fixations matérielles qui empêchent les glisses de skateboard, BMX et patins en ligne sur les propriétés commerciales et municipales canadiennes. Notre variante à plots est la gamme la plus spécifiée — fixation de surface, inox 316L grade marin, conçu pour les cycles gel-dégel. \n\n## Matériaux et finitions pour le climat canadien\n\nLes villes côtières comme **Vancouver, Halifax et Victoria** exigent l'**inox 316 grade marin** parce que la corrosion par chlorure de l'air salin détruit l'inox 304 en 5 à 7 ans. Les déploiements intérieurs à **Toronto, Calgary, Winnipeg et Edmonton** utilisent l'**inox 304** avec une finition brossée qui dissimule les éraflures. Pour les sites patrimoniaux — **Vieux-Montréal, Colline du Parlement, Citadelle de Halifax, Inner Harbour Victoria** — nous offrons une **finition patine bronze** approuvée par les agents de conservation patrimoniale.\n\n## Modèles d'installation par type de surface\n\nPour les **murs de bacs et de soutènement en béton**, nous ancrons avec des **chevilles à expansion en inox 3/8\\\" × 3 pouces** percées à **75 mm** de profondeur. Les **rebords en granite et calcaire** utilisent des **inserts filetés en inox** dans des carottages de 12 mm — aucune tache de surface. Les **bancs de maçonnerie chapeautés de bois** reçoivent des **vis à bois en inox #14 × 65 mm**. Chaque installation inclut un **scellement de calfeutrage post-installation** résistant aux cycles gel-dégel canadiens jusqu'à **-40 °C**.\n\n## Ce que ce produit n'est pas\n\nLes plots ne conviennent **pas** aux mains courantes rondes (utilisez plutôt nos **serrages de main courante**) ni aux surfaces de moins de **80 mm** de largeur (utilisez les **bandes**).",
